+# =============================================================================
+# ON COMPARING THIS WITH f1tenth_gym
+#
+# Worth being precise, because the comparison is easy to overclaim.
+#
+# f1tenth_gym is better at, and this does not attempt: vehicle dynamics (tyre
+# model, slip, actual drivetrain), full-resolution lidar, racing lines,
+# lap timing, and any question about how a car handles.
+#
+# This is better at, and f1tenth_gym cannot do: more than two agents, the
+# network as a modelled object, link quality as a measured signal, a bounded
+# arena matching a real room, heterogeneous platforms in one world, and
+# parameters that carry their sources.
+#
+# So the honest claim is not "better simulator". It is: the two answer
+# different questions, and nothing open answers the second one for a mixed
+# air/ground fleet. Run both, and the comparison that means something is
+# whether the network-layer effects seen here are absent there - because that
+# absence is the gap this exists to fill.
+# =============================================================================
