+# =============================================================================
+# Deadband MAP — lab_box
+# =============================================================================
+# A MAP is the WORLD, with no tasking in it: the arena, the radios, the agents'
+# bodies and spawn points, and named POINTS OF INTEREST. It says nothing about
+# what the agents are trying to do - that is a MISSION, and any mission that
+# refers only to points this map defines can be run here.
+#
+# A mission loads a map by name:   map: lab_box   ->   maps/lab_box.yaml
+#
+# POINTS are the bridge that makes a mission portable. A mission says "shuttle
+# between A and B"; this map says where A and B actually are. Drop the same
+# mission on a different map that also defines A and B, and it runs there with
+# no edit. Points are named in UPPER CASE by convention so they read as
+# landmarks, not variables.
+#
+# THE PROVENANCE RULE still applies: every physical quantity is {value, unit,
+# source}. An empty source is allowed but counted and flagged. Never invent one.
+#
+# CONVENTION: pose.z is the BASE of an agent (its ground contact).
+# =============================================================================
+
+spec_version: 0.1
+name: big_hall
+kind: map
+description: >
+  The lab: an 8x8 bounded indoor box, three RoboRacer bodies plus a ground
+  station, one 2.4 GHz network. Points A-F mark the ends of the three lanes.
+
+
+# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# ARENA
+# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+arena:
+  type: box
+  extent:
+    x: 12.0
+    y: 10.0
+    z: 3.0                     # a room, not a cube - ceiling height
+
+  # What the lidar sees when a beam lands on a wall. The datasheet gives 10 m
+  # against a white Kent sheet and 4 m at 10% diffuse reflectance, so the
